      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be a great addition even for non full body tracking. With some avatars, they simply can not touch the ground at real height.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-08-19T15:42:27.203Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "One of the tricks used to make fullbody avatars work between avatars of different proportions and us users with different proportions, is to change our in-game height until it matches our torso and then use playspace mover to align the trackers to our hips/feet.\n\nKung has a good tutorial showcasing what this hacky method is like:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IqUVFuSD5a4\n\nThe thing is, lots of avatars have different proportions, and it's not a simple task for everyone to just learn how to edit models to personally re-scale models to their own proportions.\n\nI have some avatars that work fine in fullbody at my normal height setting, some where I have to set my height to a whole foot lower, some a couple of inches lower. Point is, it varies depending on the avatar.\n\nIt'd be cool if I could assign a height to specific avatars so that I don't need to remember all the different values for different avatars I use.\n\n...\n\nOf course, that would be simply streamlining our hacky workaround for making fullbody avatars work in a reasonable way, and would be somewhat of \"strange wording\" to have per-avatar settings for our \"irl height\".\n\nThe real solution to this problem would be if the system better supported fullbody (across a variety of differently scaled avatars) in a more inherent way.",
